CORE
main.c
--arch x86_64 --unwind 5 --unwinding-assertions
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
inline assembly not understood
--
A sub-register input operand that is a known constant must stay a constant
after the asm is lowered. Before the fix the input was merged into an
uninitialised register temporary, so the lock word became symbolic and both
spin loops unwound to the bound; the outer loop is fully unwound here (five
iterations cover the four spin_lock/spin_unlock calls) so any remaining
unwinding-assertion failure would come from an unresolved spin loop. With the
fix the input is zero-extended and stays concrete, the spin loops resolve to a
single iteration, and verification succeeds.
